                            <comment id="16757438" author="rkondakov" created="Thu, 31 Jan 2019 16:23:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The root cause of the bug was the case when get request is mapped to the node with partition which is being preloaded (partition is not in the &lt;tt&gt;OWNING&lt;/tt&gt; state), this causes a &lt;tt&gt;ForceKeyRequest&lt;/tt&gt; to the supplier. This request is not supported by MVCC caches, even more, there are intentions to get rid of it for non-MVCC caches too (&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-10251&quot; title=&quot;Get rid of the code left from times when lateAffinity=false was supported&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-10251&quot;&gt;IGNITE-10251&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;br/&gt;
So the decision is to prohibit &lt;tt&gt;ForceKeyRequest&lt;/tt&gt; for MVCC caches and send error back to the near node if partition is not in the &lt;tt&gt;OWNING&lt;/tt&gt; state. In this case near node resends request to the next affinity node to obtain a value, until the &lt;tt&gt;OWNING&lt;/tt&gt; partition is found.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
